 Begin!"}]}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "New task:\n# Canonical dependency paths and deterministic build order\n\nOnly modify `paths.py` and `graph.py`. Standard library Python only.\n\n`paths.canonical_path(value)` accepts a str describing a relative POSIX path.\nCollapse empty components, '.' and internal '..'; reject any '..' that would\nescape the root. Reject empty final path, leading '/', any backslash, any colon\nand any NUL. Non-str raises TypeError; other invalid input raises ValueError.\nDo not access the filesystem. Leading/trailing spaces are ordinary path content\nand must be preserved. Example a//b/../c -> a/c, ../a invalid, a/.. invalid.\n\n`graph.build_order(graph)` accepts a dict mapping path strings to lists of their\ndependency path strings. Canonicalize every key/dependency. Multiple keys that\ncanonicalize to one node merge their dependency sets; duplicate dependencies\nare ignored. Every dependency must be a declared canonical key, otherwise raise\nValueError. Return each canonical node exactly once, with all dependencies\nbefore it. At each step choose the lexicographically smallest currently available\nnode (Python str order). A cycle, including a self edge after normalization,\nraises ValueError. Empty graph -> []. Validate input type: graph must be dict\nand each dependency collection must be list; otherwise TypeError. Preserve inputs.\n\nCreate a plan, fully read both editable files, and run `python -m pytest -q`\nbefore any write. After the final edit run full `python -m pytest -q`, then mark\nthe plan done and final_answer normally on success. Never modify test files.\n\n\nCourse execution contract:\n{\"profile\": \"generic\", \"editable\": [\"graph.py\", \"paths.py\"], \"required_full_reads\": [\"graph.py\", \"paths.py\"], \"verify_commands\": [[\"python\", \"-m\", \"pytest\", \"-q\"]], \"required_pages\": [], \"note_topics\": [], \"max_model_calls\": 20}\nUse update_plan before editing, run baseline checks, then read the required files with read_file.\nTools return Python dicts; use their file_hash for expected_hash. Variables persist across actions.\nDo not reset a successful plan or repeat completed baseline checks. Continue the next unfinished action.\nAll writes and tests must use these tools. Call final_answer only after current-file verification.\nos and pathlib are unavailable in action code; use file/command tools. Import allowed modules before using them.\n\nCurrent plan; retain these exact titles and order, update status only:\n[{\"title\": \"Run baseline test suite\", \"status\": \"doing\"}, {\"title\": \"Fully read graph.py and paths.py\", \"status\": \"todo\"}, {\"title\": \"Implement canonical_path and build_order\", \"status\": \"todo\"}, {\"title\": \"Run full verification tests\", \"status\": \"todo\"}, {\"title\": \"Finalize plan and answer\", \"status\": \"todo\"}]\nCourse progress before this request (evidence offered below may satisfy pending items after delivery):\n{\"phase\":\"read\",\"next_requirement\":\"read_file: graph.py\",\"remaining_count\":5,\"requests_left\":17,\"baseline_done\":1,\"changed_files\":[],\"verified_current\":0,\"required_checks\":1,\"request_number\":3,\"max_requests\":20,\"requests_after_response\":17}"}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I’ll initialize the plan, then run the baseline test command before any file writes.\n\n```python\nplan = update_plan(items=[\n    {\"title\": \"Run baseline test suite\", \"status\": \"doing\"},\n    {\"title\": \"Fully read graph.py and paths.py\", \"status\": \"todo\"},\n    {\"title\": \"Implement canonical_path and build_order\", \"status\": \"todo\"},\n    {\"title\": \"Run full verification tests\", \"status\": \"todo\"},\n    {\"title\": \"Finalize plan and answer\", \"status\": \"todo\"},\n])\nprint(plan)\n\nbaseline = run_command(argv=[\"python\", \"-m\", \"pytest\", \"-q\"], cwd=\".\")\nprint(baseline)\n```\n"}]}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type":